invariant: INV-14
file: srv_resume.c
catches: srv_flight_test
reason: the lifetime check measures the distance between the two instants in
  either direction, so a ticket dated after the server's clock resumes.
  A ticket this server issued can only carry a later instant when the
  clocks of the servers sharing the key disagree or the key has leaked,
  and either way the ticket's lifetime is no longer measured from a time
  the server has seen. test/srv_resume_tests.h offers a ticket one second
  in the future and requires it to be passed over.

--- old
    return now_seconds >= auth_seconds && now_seconds - auth_seconds <= SRV_TICKET_LIFETIME;
--- new
    uint64_t apart =
        now_seconds >= auth_seconds ? now_seconds - auth_seconds : auth_seconds - now_seconds;
    return apart <= SRV_TICKET_LIFETIME;
